# Universe content · life · fungi (domain Eukaryotes, kingdom Fungi)
# researched: OpenStax Biology 2e "24.2 Classifications of Fungi"; Pearson study guide on fungal diversity
#   and life cycles; standard biology for lichens, root partners and decomposers
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r08-life-sim.md

# ── Phyla ──

@phylum chytrids
name: Chytrids
real: yes
kingdom: fungi
says: the only fungi that still swim with a tail; mostly in water; one kind is killing frogs worldwide

@phylum zygomycetes
name: Zygomycetes (Mucoromycota)
real: yes
kingdom: fungi
example: bread mold
says: fast molds on fruit and bread

@phylum glomeromycetes
name: Glomeromycetes
real: yes
kingdom: fungi
says: root partners living inside most plants' roots, trading minerals for sugar

@phylum ascomycetes
name: Sac fungi (Ascomycota)
real: yes
kingdom: fungi
says: the biggest group: yeasts, molds, morels and truffles

@phylum basidiomycetes
name: Club fungi (Basidiomycota)
real: yes
kingdom: fungi
says: mushrooms with gills, puffballs, and the rusts and smuts that attack crops

# ── Body parts ──

@part hypha
name: Hypha
real: yes
says: a thin thread, the basic body of a fungus

@part mycelium
name: Mycelium
real: yes
says: a hidden web of threads through soil, wood or flesh; one can spread for kilometers

@part fruiting-body
name: Fruiting body
real: yes
says: the mushroom or cup that pops up to release spores

@part spores
name: Spores
real: yes
says: tiny seeds of a fungus, carried by wind, water and animals

@part gills
name: Gills
real: yes
says: the thin plates under a mushroom cap where spores are made

# ── Ways of living ──

@life decomposer
name: Decomposer
real: yes
says: rots dead plants and animals back into soil

@life root-partner
name: Root partner (mycorrhiza)
real: yes
says: wraps or enters plant roots, trading water and minerals for sugar; links plants into networks

@life lichen
name: Lichen
real: yes
says: a fungus and an alga living as one, able to grow on bare rock

@life parasite
name: Parasite
real: yes
says: feeds on living plants, insects or animals

@life mind-control
name: Body-snatching fungus
real: yes
says: takes over an insect's behavior before killing it

@life yeast
name: Yeast
real: yes
says: single-celled fungi that ferment sugar into alcohol and gas

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule fungi-recyclers
real: rule
says: fungi rot what dies and return it to the soil; without them dead matter piles up

@rule fungi-networks
real: rule
says: root-partner fungi link plants underground, sharing food and warnings (the root-network step on the grouping ladder)

@rule fungi-spread
real: rule
says: fungi spread by spores on wind and water, and by growing their mycelium through soil and wood

@rule fungi-land
real: rule
says: root-partner fungi help the first plants move onto land

@rule fungi-farming
real: rule
says: fungi can be farmed: by ants and termites, and by thinking species for food, drugs and fermenting
